    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The build passes green. All changes complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI changed owner deletion from a hard delete to a soft delete.\n\n**What changed:**\n\n1. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a `deleted` field (primitive `boolean`, defaults `false`) mapped to a new `deleted` column, with `isDeleted()`/`setDeleted()` accessors.\n\n2. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `deleted` boolean property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct auto-maps it (matching name).\n\n3. **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**\n   - `deleteOwner`: instead of removing the record, it sets `deleted = true` and saves the owner, still returning `204 No Content` (2xx). The row is retained, so `GET` still returns it with `deleted: true`.\n   - The create endpoint's blocking **identity** check and **household duplicate** check now filter out `existing.isDeleted()` owners, and the soft **possible-duplicate** detection does the same. A normally-blocking duplicate is thus allowed when the only match is soft-deleted.\n   - Newly created owners have `deleted` false (entity default; never set true except on delete).\n\n4. **DB schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 Added the `deleted` column with a `DEFAULT FALSE NOT NULL` (`BIT DEFAULT 0` for MySQL) so existing seed inserts remain valid and load as not-deleted. Tests run on hsqldb with `ddl-auto=none`, so the schema column was required.\n\n**Tests:** `./mvnw -o test` \u2192 `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**. Both new acceptance tests (`coreSoftDeleteFlagsAndRetains`, `coreDeletedOwnerIgnoredByDuplicateCheck`) pass.",
